{"operations":[{"content":"The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment adopted 2 May 2026. [[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]\n\nWhere the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies. [[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]\n","expected_sha256":"90ef3448573a604a15ed0ada6b611c7018da9a8618a39de94fda5a6784eec017","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Removed the statement about the bylaws stating one half quorum to avoid forbidden claims; kept only the amendment's quorum and the precedence statement, both supported by the amendment source."}